{"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "prove", "attempt": 1, "request": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling\n\nImplement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function. Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values. Use Python standard library only, no external I/O. Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end. Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events. For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,... strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)). Sum only non-null in-range values; count counts these values. A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value. Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first); empty buckets never reset previous. Events before start never seed previous. Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order. Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.\n\nImplement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.\n\nPublic examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]\n", "clauses": [{"clause_id": "C1", "quote": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling", "refs": []}, {"clause_id": "C2", "quote": "Implement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C3", "quote": "Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C4", "quote": "Use Python standard library only, no external I/O.", "refs": ["R1"]}, {"clause_id": "C5", "quote": "Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C6", "quote": "Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C7", "quote": "For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C8", "quote": "strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C9", "quote": "Sum only non-null in-range values;", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C10", "quote": "count counts these values.", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C11", "quote": "A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.", "refs": ["O5", "I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C12", "quote": "Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first);", "refs": ["O5"]}, {"clause_id": "C13", "quote": "empty buckets never reset previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C14", "quote": "Events before start never seed previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C15", "quote": "Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C16", "quote": "Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.", "refs": ["O4", "I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C17", "quote": "Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C18", "quote": "Use only the standard library, no external I/O.", "refs": ["R1"]}, {"clause_id": "C19", "quote": "The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C20", "quote": "Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C21", "quote": "Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]", "refs": ["O7"]}], "records": [{"id": "D1", "revision": 1, "kind": "entity", "role": "declaration", "statement": "Input is an object containing events, start, end, width and fill. Each event has a string group, integer time and integer or null value; start and end are integers, width is a positive integer, fill is 'none' or 'previous', and start <= end.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 366, "interpretation": "Specified input structure and domain.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 238}], "scope": ["input domain"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["The specified input fields and types define the supported domain, including empty events and start = end."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:437dbab2e3029e5e51c2c75cbf69cdff7ec470ca52d5afd31fd4eb6d3e7b37d3", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O1", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Provide a pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) function in solution.py accepting JSON-compatible Python input and returning a JSON-serializable result.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 134, "interpretation": "Required function and purity.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 79}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 186, "interpretation": "JSON-compatible interface.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 135}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1129, "interpretation": "Python 3 and deterministic purity.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1053}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1251, "interpretation": "JSON input and serializable output.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1178}], "scope": ["function interface and execution"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["solution.py exposes solve(data).", "Repeated calls with equal input return equal results.", "The function has no externally observable side effects and does not mutate its input.", "The result is JSON-serializable."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:9c3de68c3af25a319ad04be9b72cbaa805ccdff263ef90186a33bbfda5cbaa5f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O2", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Derive groups from all unique event group names and sort them lexicographically, including groups whose events all fall outside the requested interval.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 474, "interpretation": "Complete group discovery and ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 367}], "scope": ["group enumeration"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Groups equal the lexicographically sorted set of group names across all input events.", "Out-of-range events still establish group membership.", "An empty event list yields no groups."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e019a37afda75f7cb0d156d81716a45f428a28813aea5734b2a3f38265a3a668", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O3", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For every group emit one bucket for each start + k*width with integer k >= 0 and bucket start strictly below end; its interval is [bucketStart, min(bucketStart + width, end)).", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 534, "interpretation": "Bucket start sequence for each group.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 475}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 610, "interpretation": "Strict stopping boundary and half-open bucket intervals.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 535}], "scope": ["bucket enumeration and boundaries"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Each group has exactly the specified bucket starts in ascending order.", "Bucket lower boundaries are inclusive and upper boundaries are exclusive.", "The last bucket is clipped at end.", "start = end yields an empty result."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:f07764143e401bea18008dfac48e768edc3d0e8241427c0da64c7eb307770802", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O4", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For each group and bucket, count and sum every matching event with non-null value whose time lies in that bucket; preserve duplicate event contributions.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 645, "interpretation": "Non-null in-range aggregation.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 611}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 672, "interpretation": "Count uses the same contributing values.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 646}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Duplicate occurrences are counted.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["bucket aggregation"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["count equals the number of non-null matching event occurrences in the bucket.", "sum equals the integer sum of those occurrences.", "Null values contribute neither to count nor sum.", "Events outside [start,end) contribute neither to count nor sum.", "Duplicate occurrences each contribute independently."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:f4536874cd19b7f051075b92e1c61916a06e52a16992c5e1af61e4f658c9c73e", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O5", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "A bucket with count > 0 returns its sum as value. A bucket with count = 0 returns null for fill 'none'; for fill 'previous' it returns the sum of the latest earlier bucket of the same group with count > 0, or null if no such bucket exists.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 732, "interpretation": "Nonempty bucket output and previous value.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 673}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 852, "interpretation": "Empty bucket behavior in both fill modes.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 733}], "scope": ["bucket values and causal filling"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Nonempty buckets return their sum for either fill mode.", "Empty buckets return null in fill 'none' mode.", "Empty buckets in fill 'previous' mode use only the latest earlier nonempty bucket of their own group.", "Before the first nonempty bucket, previous-filled values are null."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e6ebb9ef8478990658a37036b756a99525de853ac2483d6cfdbf9bf6126e574f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O6", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Return a list of records with group, start, count and value fields, ordered first by lexicographically sorted group and then by ascending bucket start, preserving the specified interface structure.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 992, "interpretation": "Output fields and record ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 930}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1317, "interpretation": "Preserve specified structure and exact ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1252}], "scope": ["output structure and ordering"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O5", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Each emitted record contains exactly group, start, count and value.", "Records follow group order and then bucket order.", "Record fields contain the group name, bucket start, contributing count and specified filled or summed value."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:8e56cb13201b730691a1da493f8704551cb36aaaef1b3e9da9dda9fff3f0679e", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O7", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Match both supplied public example outputs exactly.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1891, "interpretation": "Concrete examples require zero propagation and prohibit pre-start seeding.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1319}], "scope": ["public examples"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O6", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "I1", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["For group a with values 2 and -2 in the first bucket, return records at starts 0, 2 and 4 with counts 2, 0 and 0 and values 0, 0 and 0.", "For group z with its only event at time -1 and start 0, return one record at start 0 with count 0 and value null."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:fdf388c03407e80a50c26c0f607a7489e1826b58a1422cc74821483be6918ffb", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "I1", "revision": 1, "kind": "invariant", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "During each group's ascending bucket traversal, previous is initially absent and changes only upon a bucket with count > 0, to that bucket's sum including zero. Empty buckets retain previous, and events before start never initialize it.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 732, "interpretation": "Nonempty buckets establish previous.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 673}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 888, "interpretation": "Empty buckets retain previous.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 853}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 929, "interpretation": "Pre-start events cannot seed filling.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 889}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Zero is a valid previous sum.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["per-group previous state"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Previous state is independent for each group.", "Empty buckets never reset previous.", "A nonempty bucket with sum zero establishes previous = 0.", "Events before start cannot seed previous."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:81718211c9dd04d2b9ccd49f7030df8a5572955a6be3305107a6ecec1356068c", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "R1", "revision": 1, "kind": "resource_constraint", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Use only Python standard-library facilities and perform no external I/O.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 237, "interpretation": "Dependency and I/O restrictions.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 187}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1177, "interpretation": "Repeated dependency and I/O restrictions.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1130}], "scope": ["implementation and function execution"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No non-standard-library dependencies are required.", "Execution performs no external I/O."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:65829cf0d1159691095c1eda4c2fb3720228eda03633ae7ba634bbf421bafb98", "blocked_by": []}], "lean_source": "import Std\n\n-- BEGIN VERISLOP REGISTRY\n-- Generated by `verislop formalize`. Typed obligation metadata: an index, never evidence.\nnamespace VeriSlop.Registry\n\nstructure SourceRef where\n  documentRef : String\n  documentHash : String\n  startByte : Nat\n  endByte : Nat\n  origin : String\n  interpretation : String\n\nstructure Dependency where\n  id : String\n  relation : String\n\nstructure Entry where\n  id : String\n  revision : Nat\n  kind : String\n  role : String\n  statement : String\n  required : Bool\n  sourceRefs : List SourceRef\n  scope : List String\n  dependencies : List Dependency\n  acceptanceCriteria : List String\n  bindings : List String\n\ndef «D1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"D1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"entity\",\n  role := \"declaration\",\n  statement := \"Input is an object containing events, start, end, width and fill. Each event has a string group, integer time and integer or null value; start and end are integers, width is a positive integer, fill is 'none' or 'previous', and start <= end.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 238, endByte := 366, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Specified input structure and domain.\" }],\n  scope := [\"input domain\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"The specified input fields and types define the supported domain, including empty events and start = end.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.Event\", \"VeriSlopAST.Input\", \"VeriSlopAST.Row\", \"VeriSlopAST.solve\"] }\n\ndef «O1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Provide a pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) function in solution.py accepting JSON-compatible Python input and returning a JSON-serializable result.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 79, endByte := 134, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Required function and purity.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 135, endByte := 186, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"JSON-compatible interface.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 1053, endByte := 1129, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Python 3 and deterministic purity.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 1178, endByte := 1251, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"JSON input and serializable output.\" }],\n  scope := [\"function interface and execution\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"solution.py exposes solve(data).\", \"Repeated calls with equal input return equal results.\", \"The function has no externally observable side effects and does not mutate its input.\", \"The result is JSON-serializable.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.python_interface\"] }\n\ndef «O2» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O2\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Derive groups from all unique event group names and sort them lexicographically, including groups whose events all fall outside the requested interval.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 367, endByte := 474, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Complete group discovery and ordering.\" }],\n  scope := [\"group enumeration\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Groups equal the lexicographically sorted set of group names across all input events.\", \"Out-of-range events still establish group membership.\", \"An empty event list yields no groups.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «O3» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O3\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"For every group emit one bucket for each start + k*width with integer k >= 0 and bucket start strictly below end; its interval is [bucketStart, min(bucketStart + width, end)).\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 475, endByte := 534, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Bucket start sequence for each group.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 535, endByte := 610, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Strict stopping boundary and half-open bucket intervals.\" }],\n  scope := [\"bucket enumeration and boundaries\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }, { id := \"O2\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Each group has exactly the specified bucket starts in ascending order.\", \"Bucket lower boundaries are inclusive and upper boundaries are exclusive.\", \"The last bucket is clipped at end.\", \"start = end yields an empty result.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «O4» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O4\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"For each group and bucket, count and sum every matching event with non-null value whose time lies in that bucket; preserve duplicate event contributions.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 611, endByte := 645, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Non-null in-range aggregation.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 646, endByte := 672, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Count uses the same contributing values.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 993, endByte := 1051, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Duplicate occurrences are counted.\" }],\n  scope := [\"bucket aggregation\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }, { id := \"O3\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"count equals the number of non-null matching event occurrences in the bucket.\", \"sum equals the integer sum of those occurrences.\", \"Null values contribute neither to count nor sum.\", \"Events outside [start,end) contribute neither to count nor sum.\", \"Duplicate occurrences each contribute independently.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «O5» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O5\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"A bucket with count > 0 returns its sum as value. A bucket with count = 0 returns null for fill 'none'; for fill 'previous' it returns the sum of the latest earlier bucket of the same group with count > 0, or null if no such bucket exists.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 673, endByte := 732, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Nonempty bucket output and previous value.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 733, endByte := 852, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Empty bucket behavior in both fill modes.\" }],\n  scope := [\"bucket values and causal filling\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }, { id := \"O4\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Nonempty buckets return their sum for either fill mode.\", \"Empty buckets return null in fill 'none' mode.\", \"Empty buckets in fill 'previous' mode use only the latest earlier nonempty bucket of their own group.\", \"Before the first nonempty bucket, previous-filled values are null.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «O6» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O6\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Return a list of records with group, start, count and value fields, ordered first by lexicographically sorted group and then by ascending bucket start, preserving the specified interface structure.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 930, endByte := 992, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Output fields and record ordering.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 1252, endByte := 1317, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Preserve specified structure and exact ordering.\" }],\n  scope := [\"output structure and ordering\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"O2\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }, { id := \"O3\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }, { id := \"O4\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }, { id := \"O5\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Each emitted record contains exactly group, start, count and value.\", \"Records follow group order and then bucket order.\", \"Record fields contain the group name, bucket start, contributing count and specified filled or summed value.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «O7» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O7\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Match both supplied public example outputs exactly.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 1319, endByte := 1891, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Concrete examples require zero propagation and prohibit pre-start seeding.\" }],\n  scope := [\"public examples\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"O6\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }, { id := \"I1\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"For group a with values 2 and -2 in the first bucket, return records at starts 0, 2 and 4 with counts 2, 0 and 0 and values 0, 0 and 0.\", \"For group z with its only event at time -1 and start 0, return one record at start 0 with count 0 and value null.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «I1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"I1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"invariant\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"During each group's ascending bucket traversal, previous is initially absent and changes only upon a bucket with count > 0, to that bucket's sum including zero. Empty buckets retain previous, and events before start never initialize it.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 673, endByte := 732, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Nonempty buckets establish previous.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 853, endByte := 888, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Empty buckets retain previous.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 889, endByte := 929, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Pre-start events cannot seed filling.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 993, endByte := 1051, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Zero is a valid previous sum.\" }],\n  scope := [\"per-group previous state\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"O4\", relation := \"uses_proof\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Previous state is independent for each group.\", \"Empty buckets never reset previous.\", \"A nonempty bucket with sum zero establishes previous = 0.\", \"Events before start cannot seed previous.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.complete_behavior\"] }\n\ndef «R1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"R1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"resource_constraint\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Use only Python standard-library facilities and perform no external I/O.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 187, endByte := 237, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Dependency and I/O restrictions.\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/D21/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296\", startByte := 1130, endByte := 1177, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Repeated dependency and I/O restrictions.\" }],\n  scope := [\"implementation and function execution\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"No non-standard-library dependencies are required.\", \"Execution performs no external I/O.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.runtime\"] }\n\ndef entries : List Entry := [«D1», «O1», «O2», «O3», «O4», «O5», «O6», «O7», «I1», «R1»]\n\nend VeriSlop.Registry\n-- END VERISLOP REGISTRY\n\n/-!\nNormative native boundary fact model, v0.2. The host Python AST-to-fact mapping\nis source-bound and TRUSTED at Tier 0. These theorems prove rules about the fact\nmodel; they do not prove the parser, CPython, ownership analysis or arbitrary\nfuture Python programs. Facts are computed by the registered source checker,\nnever supplied as observations by a candidate author.\n-/\nnamespace VeriSlop.Native\n\ninductive NativeRequirement where\n  | entry (file qualname : String) (arity : Nat)\n  | pureJson\n  | standardRuntimeOnly\n  | noExternalIO\n  | inputPreserved\n  | deterministic\n  | noFloatingPoint\n  deriving DecidableEq\n\nstructure Entry where\n  file : String\n  qualname : String\n  arity : Nat\n  deriving DecidableEq\n\nstructure ModuleFacts where\n  entries : List Entry\n  uniqueFunctions : Bool\n  closedNames : Bool\n  acyclicCalls : Bool\n  pureJson : Bool\n  standardRuntimeOnly : Bool\n  noExternalIO : Bool\n  inputPreserved : Bool\n  deterministic : Bool\n  noFloatingPoint : Bool\n\ndef checkRequirement (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Bool :=\n  match r with\n  | .entry f n a => m.uniqueFunctions && decide (Entry.mk f n a ∈ m.entries)\n  | .pureJson => m.closedNames && m.acyclicCalls && m.pureJson\n  | .standardRuntimeOnly => m.standardRuntimeOnly\n  | .noExternalIO => m.noExternalIO\n  | .inputPreserved => m.inputPreserved\n  | .deterministic => m.deterministic\n  | .noFloatingPoint => m.noFloatingPoint\n\ndef HoldsRequirement (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Prop :=\n  match r with\n  | .entry f n a => m.uniqueFunctions = true ∧ Entry.mk f n a ∈ m.entries\n  | .pureJson => m.closedNames = true ∧ m.acyclicCalls = true ∧ m.pureJson = true\n  | .standardRuntimeOnly => m.standardRuntimeOnly = true\n  | .noExternalIO => m.noExternalIO = true\n  | .inputPreserved => m.inputPreserved = true\n  | .deterministic => m.deterministic = true\n  | .noFloatingPoint => m.noFloatingPoint = true\n\ndef checkBoundary (rs : List NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Bool :=\n  rs.all (fun r => checkRequirement r m)\n\ndef HoldsBoundary (rs : List NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Prop :=\n  ∀ r ∈ rs, HoldsRequirement r m\n\ndef Transfer (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Prop :=\n  ∀ m, checkBoundary rs m = true → HoldsBoundary rs m\n\ndef AdmissionInhabited (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Prop :=\n  ∃ m, checkBoundary rs m = true\n\n-- The endpoint is real closed Lean data containing the accepted function.\n-- Its identity is reified and linked independently; the boundary theorem does\n-- not establish functional equivalence to this reference implementation.\nstructure NativeDefinition (τ : Type) where\n  endpoint : τ\n  requirements : List NativeRequirement\n\ndef Contract {τ : Type} (d : NativeDefinition τ) : Prop :=\n  Transfer d.requirements ∧ AdmissionInhabited d.requirements\n\ntheorem checkRequirement_sound (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) :\n    checkRequirement r m = true → HoldsRequirement r m := by\n  cases r <;> simp [checkRequirement, HoldsRequirement, Bool.and_eq_true] <;> grind\n\ntheorem transfer_sound (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Transfer rs := by\n  intro m h r hr\n  exact checkRequirement_sound r m ((List.all_eq_true.mp h) r hr)\n\ndef witnessEntries : List NativeRequirement → List Entry\n  | [] => []\n  | .entry f n a :: rs => Entry.mk f n a :: witnessEntries rs\n  | _ :: rs => witnessEntries rs\n\ndef modelWitness (rs : List NativeRequirement) : ModuleFacts :=\n  ⟨witnessEntries rs, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true⟩\n\ntheorem entry_in_witness (f n : String) (a : Nat) (rs : List NativeRequirement)\n    (h : NativeRequirement.entry f n a ∈ rs) : Entry.mk f n a ∈ witnessEntries rs := by\n  induction rs with\n  | nil => simp at h\n  | cons r rs ih => cases r <;> simp_all [witnessEntries] <;> grind\n\ntheorem admission_inhabited (rs : List NativeRequirement) : AdmissionInhabited rs := by\n  refine ⟨modelWitness rs, List.all_eq_true.mpr ?_⟩\n  intro r hr\n  cases r with\n  | entry f n a =>\n    simp [checkRequirement, modelWitness, entry_in_witness f n a rs hr]\n  | pureJson => rfl\n  | standardRuntimeOnly => rfl\n  | noExternalIO => rfl\n  | inputPreserved => rfl\n  | deterministic => rfl\n  | noFloatingPoint => rfl\n\ntheorem contract_sound {τ : Type} (d : NativeDefinition τ) : Contract d :=\n  ⟨transfer_sound d.requirements, admission_inhabited d.requirements⟩\n\nend VeriSlop.Native\n\nnamespace VeriSlopAST\nstructure «Event» where\n  «group» : _root_.String\n  «time» : _root_.Int\n  «value» : (_root_.Option _root_.Int)\nstructure «Input» where\n  «events» : (_root_.List _root_.VeriSlopAST.«Event»)\n  «start» : _root_.Int\n  «end» : _root_.Int\n  «width» : _root_.Int\n  «fill» : _root_.String\nstructure «Row» where\n  «group» : _root_.String\n  «start» : _root_.Int\n  «count» : _root_.Nat\n  «value» : (_root_.Option _root_.Int)\nstructure «State» where\n  «rows» : (_root_.List _root_.VeriSlopAST.«Row»)\n  «previous» : (_root_.Option _root_.Int)\nstructure «Stats» where\n  «group» : _root_.St